---
/*
 * Broker candour — B2B 상품 지면. (seoulmarkets.com/data/broker-candour)
 *
 * 왜 (사장님 데이터 상품 사업): 대형 벤더는 「리포트」를 판다. 우리가 파는 것은 「의견 인플레이션의
 *   구조」 — 매도의견이 사라졌고, 그게 증권사마다 어떻게 다른가. 퀀트·리스크·미디어·규제가 산다.
 *   ⛔ 값은 지면에 안 넣는다(사장님 확정 대기). 결제 안 붙인다 — 살 뜻만 센다. ⛔ noAds(자료 지면).
 *
 * ⚠ 투자자문 아님: 등급 분포라는 **사실**이다. 「어느 증권사를 믿어라/피하라」가 아니다.
 *   목표주가가 맞았나는 P7(target-price accuracy)이 따로 잰다 — 여긴 등급만. 그 경계를 화면에 못박는다.
 *
 * 자료: src/data/broker-candour.json (scripts/build-broker-candour.mjs 산출).
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../consts';
import data from '../../data/broker-candour.json';

const m = data.market;
const rows = data.by_house;
const years = data.sell_by_year;
const TITLE = 'The Sell rating that vanished';
const SAMPLE = `${m.reports.toLocaleString()} broker reports · ${m.houses_shown} houses · ${data.year}`;
const DESC =
  'Korean broker research by rating, house by house: Buy on four in five reports, Sell on almost none. '
  + 'Of the houses we track, most issued no Sell rating at all this year. Ratings as filed — not advice.';

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: 'Korean broker rating distribution by house',
  description: DESC, url: `${SITE_URL}/data/broker-candour`,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'SeoulMarkets', url: SITE_URL },
  variableMeasured: ['Buy share', 'Hold share', 'Sell share', 'by brokerage'],
};
---

<Base title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} noAds>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="pp">
      <p class="kicker">SeoulMarkets · data for licence</p>
      <h1>The Sell rating that vanished</h1>
      <p class="sample">{SAMPLE}</p>
      <p class="lead">
        Korean brokerages rate the stocks they cover, and the rating is almost always the same one.
        Across {m.reports.toLocaleString()} reports in {data.year} the market ran <b>Buy on
        {' '}{m.buy_pct}%</b> and <b>Sell on {m.sell_pct}%</b>. House by house it barely moves: of the
        {' '}{m.houses_shown} brokerages that rated at least 200 reports, <b>{m.houses_with_zero_sell}
        issued not a single Sell all year.</b>
      </p>

      <aside class="caveat" role="note">
        <b>Read this first.</b> This is the distribution of ratings <i>as filed</i> — a market-structure
        fact, not investment advice. It is not a verdict on any brokerage, and it is neither a buy nor a
        sell signal. Whether a house's price targets actually came true is a <i>different</i> dataset —
        our <a href="/data/target-price-accuracy">target-price accuracy</a> panel. This page is about
        the rating, not whether it was right.
      </aside>

      <ol class="five">
        <li><b>What it is</b> — for each brokerage, the share of its reports rated Buy, Hold and Sell,
          plus the market total and the Sell rate by year.</li>
        <li><b>Why trust it</b> — every rating is read from a filed, dated broker note we archived, and
          grouped by the words the house itself used.</li>
        <li><b>How big</b> — {m.reports.toLocaleString()} rated reports across {m.houses_shown} houses in
          {data.year}, and a Sell-rate series back more than a decade.</li>
        <li><b>The honest caveat</b> — houses that issue no rating at all (IR bulletins) are excluded;
          shown houses filed at least 200 reports and rate the majority of them.</li>
        <li><b>The form</b> — one CSV: house · reports · Buy% · Hold% · Sell% · rated share. Plus the
          market total and the by-year Sell series.</li>
      </ol>

      <section class="blk">
        <h2>① Rating mix, by house</h2>
        <p>Ranked by Sell rate. It is a short axis: the busiest houses cluster at Buy nine-in-ten, and
          the Sell column is a row of zeros.</p>
        <div class="scroll-x">
          <table class="press">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Brokerage</th><th class="r">Reports</th><th class="r">Buy</th>
                <th class="r">Hold</th><th class="r">Sell</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {rows.map((r) => (
                <tr>
                  <td class="axis">{r.house}</td>
                  <td class="r">{r.reports}</td>
                  <td class="r">{r.buy_pct}%</td>
                  <td class="r">{r.hold_pct}%</td>
                  <td class="r"><b>{r.sell_pct}%</b></td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="fine">
          The most Buy-heavy house rated {rows[0]?.buy_pct}% of its reports Buy with no Sell at all. The
          few non-zero Sell rates in the table round to a fraction of one percent. Hold, the polite
          alternative to Sell, has all but disappeared too.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="blk">
        <h2>② The Sell rate did not fall — it was already gone</h2>
        <p>Across the whole archive the market Sell rate has sat near zero for over a decade. This is
          not a recent shift; it is the standing shape of Korean retail research.</p>
        <div class="scroll-x">
          <table class="press">
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Year</th><th class="r">Reports</th><th class="r">Sell rate</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {years.map((y) => (
                <tr class={y.year === data.year ? 'edge' : ''}>
                  <td class="axis">{y.year}</td>
                  <td class="r">{y.reports.toLocaleString()}</td>
                  <td class="r">{y.sell_pct}%</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="blk">
        <h2>③ What you get</h2>
        <table class="kv">
          <tbody>
            <tr><th>Files</th><td colspan="2">One CSV — house · reports · Buy% · Hold% · Sell% · rated
              share. Plus the market total and the by-year Sell series back more than a decade.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>The grouping</th><td colspan="2">Ratings grouped Buy / Hold / Sell from the words each
              house filed (매수·중립·매도 and their English equivalents). Notes with no rating fall to
              "other" and are not counted as any of the three.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Who is shown</th><td colspan="2">Houses with at least 200 reports in the year that
              rate the majority of them. Rating-free IR bulletins are excluded.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Not accuracy</th><td colspan="2">This is the rating, not whether it was right. Target
              accuracy is our separate <a href="/data/target-price-accuracy">price-target panel</a>.</td></tr>
            <tr><th>Source</th><td colspan="2">Our own daily archive of broker research boards.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section class="cta">
        <h2>Ask for the dataset</h2>
        <p class="cta__lead">
          Want the full by-house rating table, or the Sell-rate series over time? Leave a work email and
          we send a sample and the current licensing terms. It reaches us directly — no account, and
          this is not the newsletter.
        </p>
        <form class="ask" method="post" action="/v1/subscribe" data-source="broker-candour">
          <label class="vh" for="ask-email">Work email</label>
          <div class="ask__row">
            <input id="ask-email" type="email" name="email" required autocomplete="email"
              inputmode="email" placeholder="you@company.com" aria-describedby="ask-note" />
            <button type="submit">Request the dataset</button>
          </div>
          <div class="hp" aria-hidden="true">
            <label for="ask-hp">Leave this field empty</label>
            <input id="ask-hp" type="text" name="hp" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />
          </div>
          <p class="ask__note" id="ask-note">We store your address and that you asked about the broker
            rating dataset. We never sell or share it.</p>
          <p class="ask__msg" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        </form>
      </section>

      <p class="fine bottom">
        From our own broker-research archive · Ratings as filed, grouped Buy/Hold/Sell · Rating, not
        accuracy (see the <a href="/data/target-price-accuracy">price-target panel</a>) · Not investment
        advice. Browse <a href="/data">all SeoulMarkets datasets</a>. See our <a href="/terms">terms of use</a> and <a href="/refund">refund policy</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (() => {
      const form = document.querySelector('form.ask');
      if (!form) return;
      const input = form.querySelector('input[name="email"]');
      const hp = form.querySelector('input[name="hp"]');
      const btn = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');
      const msg = form.querySelector('.ask__msg');
      const say = (state, text) => { msg.dataset.state = state; msg.textContent = text; };
      form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
        e.preventDefault();
        const email = input.value.trim();
        if (!email) return;
        btn.disabled = true; const was = btn.textContent; btn.textContent = 'Sending…';
        delete msg.dataset.state;
        try {
          const res = await fetch('/v1/subscribe', {
            method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ email, hp: hp.value, source: form.dataset.source || 'broker-candour' }),
          });
          const d = await res.json().catch(() => ({}));
          if (res.ok && d.ok) { say('ok', 'Thanks — we have your address and will email you the sample and the terms.'); form.reset(); }
          else { say('error', d?.error?.message || d?.message || 'Could not send. Please try again.'); }
        } catch { say('error', 'Network error. Please try again.'); }
        finally { btn.disabled = false; btn.textContent = was; }
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Base>

<style>
  .pp { max-width: 46rem; margin: 0 auto; }
  .kicker { font-size: .74rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .08em; color: var(--accent);
            font-weight: 700; margin: 1.2rem 0 .3rem; }
  .pp h1 { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 5vw, 2.4rem); line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 .5rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .pp .sample { font-size: .9rem; color: var(--muted); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
                margin: 0 0 1.4rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .pp .lead { font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 1.4rem; }
  .pp .lead b { font-weight: 650; }
  .caveat { margin: 0 0 1.8rem; padding: .9rem 1.1rem; border: 1px solid var(--accent);
            border-radius: 8px; background: var(--accent-soft, var(--card)); font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.65; }
  .caveat b { color: var(--ink); }
  .five { margin: 0 0 2.4rem; padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem 1.1rem 2.4rem; background: var(--card);
          border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 8px; }
  .five li { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: .92rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .five li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .five li b { color: var(--ink); }
  .blk { margin: 0 0 2.2rem; }
  .blk h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .blk p { line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }
  .scroll-x { overflow-x: auto; }
  table.kv, table.press { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .9rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }
  table.kv th, table.kv td, table.press th, table.press td {
    padding: .55rem .6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  table.kv th { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; width: 1%; }
  table.kv td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  table.kv td[colspan] { white-space: normal; line-height: 1.6; font-variant-numeric: normal; }
  table.press th { font-size: .74rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .04em;
                   color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  table.press td.axis { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); white-space: nowrap; }
  table.press tr.edge td { background: var(--accent-soft, var(--card)); }
  .r { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  code { font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace); font-size: .86em;
         background: var(--card); padding: .1em .35em; border-radius: 4px; }
  .cta { margin: 2.4rem 0 0; padding: 1.3rem 1.3rem; border: 1px solid var(--line);
         border-radius: 10px; background: var(--card); }
  .cta h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
  .cta p { line-height: 1.7; font-size: .95rem; }
  .cta__lead { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .cta a, .pp a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid currentColor; padding-bottom: 1px; }
  .cta a:hover, .pp a:hover { color: var(--ink); }
  .vh { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); clip-path: inset(50%); white-space: nowrap; }
  .ask__row { display: flex; gap: .5rem; max-width: 30rem; }
  .ask__row input { flex: 1 1 auto; min-width: 0; font: inherit; font-size: .95rem; padding: .6rem .7rem;
    color: var(--ink); background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; }
  .ask__row input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; border-color: var(--accent); }
  .ask__row button { flex: 0 0 auto; font: inherit; font-size: .92rem; font-weight: 650; cursor: pointer;
    padding: .6rem 1rem; color: var(--bg); background: var(--ink); border: 1px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 6px; }
  .ask__row button:hover { opacity: .9; }
  .ask__row button[disabled] { opacity: .6; cursor: default; }
  .hp { position: absolute; left: -9999px; width: 1px; height: 1px; overflow: hidden; }
  .ask__note { margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }
  .ask__msg { margin: .6rem 0 0; font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.55; display: none; }
  .ask__msg[data-state] { display: block; }
  .ask__msg[data-state='ok'] { color: var(--up, #1a7f37); }
  .ask__msg[data-state='error'] { color: var(--down, #c0392b); }
  @media (max-width: 30rem) { .ask__row { flex-direction: column; } .ask__row button { width: 100%; } }
  .fine { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; }
  .fine.bottom { margin: 2.4rem 0 1rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { table.kv th { white-space: normal; } .pp .sample { white-space: normal; } }
</style>
